From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 16:50:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] usb: roles: Add the Apple S8000 Lightning port role switch

The A9 USB complex pairs a device-only DWC2 with a separate EHCI + OHCI
host pair behind one AUSB PHY. On the iPad 5 the Lightning port is a USB
device by default; the camera adapter needs it to be a host.

Add a usb_role switch for the port. Device mode stays the default and
needs no register access. Host mode follows the iOS order: soft-
disconnect the gadget (it stays bound, as iOS keeps the device
controller published), make sure the complex's DMA remap words for the
host pair are set, power the PHY, create EHCI and then OHCI from the
switch's child nodes so that their power domains are on, set USB_CTL bit
1 and then host select, and switch the PHY to its host tunables. Leaving
host mode undoes the steps in reverse and reconnects the gadget, which
comes on once the device controller's own role allows it (the Lightning
charger sets that role).

A host role is entered on request through /sys/class/usb_role and lasts
until the device role is requested. The Lightning accessory policy in
the Tristar charger can claim a host entry for an accessory, through
<linux/usb/apple-s8000-role.h>. For such an entry, and before the
policy's ID-bus identification, the switch powers the accessory as iOS
does: it routes the Tristar ACC pin to the power rail and the data lanes
for USB (ACC_CTRL 0x30 and dxctrl 0xa1 for the adapter in orientation 1,
through an intermediate dxctrl byte when a lane pair changes), then
enables the PMIC's accessory LDO, its switch and its sleep enable. The
Tristar bytes it found are restored when the power goes off. The policy
also samples the Tristar through the switch, so that no role change
overlaps the sample. System sleep is refused in the host role.

The camera adapter sequence was exercised on an iPad 5 with an earlier
kernel. This shared-driver integration still needs hardware validation.

Assisted-by: LLM
